## 6) SEO architecture for Sādhaka (what to build)

### 6.1 Core principle: build an “Entity Graph + Page Factory”
Competitors that win at scale (Insight Timer, Art of Living, Isha) do some version of:
- define entities (topics/practices/teachers/traditions)
- define relationships
- generate many consistent pages

**Proposed entity types**
- `Tradition` (e.g., Vedanta, Bhakti, Tantra, Kriya, Yoga, Buddhism, Jain, Sikh spirituality)
- `Practice` (asana, pranayama, japa, trataka, nyasa, meditation styles, etc.)
- `Text` (Gita, Yoga Sutras, Upanishads, etc.)
- `Teacher/Lineage` (as neutral “influencer/teacher” entities; avoid claiming authority)
- `Goal/Intent` (sleep, anxiety, focus, devotion, self-inquiry, etc.)
- `Ritual/Festival` (Navratri, Maha Shivaratri, etc.)
- `Place` (only if you genuinely have location relevance: retreats, centers, events)

### 6.2 Page types (MVP → scale)
**MVP (highest ROI)**
1. `/spiritual-paths/{path}` (Sādhaka’s unique differentiator; “Faith Finder” output pages)
2. `/practices/{practice}` (what/why/how)
3. `/topics/{topic}` (hub pages like Insight Timer)[cite:77]
4. `/traditions/{tradition}` (overview + internal linking)
5. `/guides/{guide}` (hand-curated cornerstone content)

**Scale pSEO (graph-driven)**
- `/practices/{practice}/for/{goal}`
- `/traditions/{tradition}/practices/{practice}`
- `/texts/{text}/themes/{theme}`
- `/compare/{x}-vs-{y}` (strictly factual + exclusion-safe)

### 6.3 Technical requirements (non-negotiable)
- SSR or prerender for all SEO routes (Next.js/Remix/Astro—anything that outputs HTML)
- Clean canonical URLs
- `robots.txt` + `sitemap.xml` (split sitemaps by type when large)
- structured data (Section 7)
- internal linking rules (Section 8)

