## 12) “How they built it” — implementation patterns to copy

### 12.1 Sitemap strategy (ship early)
- `sitemap_index.xml`
  - `sitemap_practices.xml`
  - `sitemap_topics.xml`
  - `sitemap_traditions.xml`
  - `sitemap_guides.xml`
  - `sitemap_paths.xml`
- Keep each < 50k URLs; split by `-1`, `-2` if needed.

### 12.2 Localization strategy (only when justified)
Art of Living scales by country sitemaps.[cite:90]  
For Sādhaka:
- start with `en` only
- add `hi` later only if you can support:
  - translated UI + translated content
  - hreflang + canonicalization rules
  - culturally appropriate wording

### 12.3 Content storage format
- Keep a structured content DB (Postgres) + export to static routes
- Or content-as-code:
  - `/content/practices/{practice}.mdx`
  - `/content/topics/{topic}.mdx`
- For pSEO at scale: store structured facts in JSON, render via templates.

